{"id":"word:hebrew:H5035","type":"word","title":"נֶבֶל","subtitle":"H5035 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a skin- bag for liquids (from collapsing when empty); hence, a vase (as similar in shape when full); also a lyre (as having a body of like form)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נֶבֶל (H5035) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 38 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נֶבֶל (nebel) means a skin- bag for liquids (from collapsing when empty); hence, a vase (as similar in shape when full); also a lyre (as having a body of like form) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 13 8."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נֶבֶל","transliteration":"nebel","pronunciation":"neh'-bel","strong":"H5035","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5035","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["בִּ/נְבָלִ֖ים","וּ/בִ/נְבָלִ֣ים","נְבָלִ֥ים","וּ/נְבָלִ֖ים","נֵ֖בֶל"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",7],["HR/Ncmpa",5],["HNcmpa",4],["HC/R/Ncmpa",3],["HTd/Ncmsa",3],["HC/Ncmpa",2],["HC/Ncmsc",2],["HNcmpc/Sp2ms",2],["HR/Ncmsc",2],["HNcmsc",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a skin- bag for liquids (from collapsing when empty); hence, a vase (as similar in shape when full); also a lyre (as having a body of like form)","usage":"bottle, pitcher, psaltery, vessel, viol.","full":"H5035. nebel I. נֵ֫בֶל noun masculine Jer 13:12 1 skin-bottle, skin ; 2 jar, pitcher ; — נֵ֫בֶל absolute 1Sam 10:5 +; construct 10:3 + (on נֶכֶל see Baer 1:24 ); — 1 skin of wine , יַיִן נֵ֫בֶל 1Sam 1:24 ; 10:3 ; 2Sam 16:1 , compare also Jer 13:12 (twice in verse); plural יַיִן נִבְלֵי 1Sam 25:18 : figurative שָׁמַיִם נִבְלֵי Job 38:37 i.e. clouds (|| שְׁחָקִים ). 2 earthen jar, pitcher: figurative of connections of Eliakim נְבָלִים כְּלֵי Isa 22:24 ; יְנַמֵּ֑צוּ נִבְלֵיהֶם Jer 48:12 (|| יָרִיקוּ כֵּלִים ) in figure of Moab (compare Psa 2:9 ); נִבְלֵיתֶֿרֶשׂ Lam 4:2 simile of men of Judah (|| יוֺצֵר יְדֵי מַעֲשֵׂה ); simile of destruction of Judah, יוֺצְרִים נֵ֫כֶל שֵׁבֶר Isa 30:14 . II. נֶ֫בֶל נֵ֫בֶל, noun masculine Psa 57:9 a musical instrument, either a portable harp , or a lute, guitar (with bulging resonance-body at lower end); (perhaps = 1. נֵבֶל , and then shape seems to favour lute ; perhaps independent word, e.g. Egyptian loan-word, compare nfr, lute , We Hpt 222 ); — absolute נֵ֫בֶל 1Sam 10:5 3 t., נֶ֫בֶל Psa 71:22 3 t.; נָ֑בֶל Amos 6:5 2 t.; plural נְבָלִים 2Sam 6:5 4 t.; suffix נְבָלֶיךָ Amos 5:23 ; Isa 14:11 ; &#8212; harp (or lute ), played at feasts and religious ceremonies, probably less simple, cheap and common than כִּנּוֺר (q. v.; often named with ׳נ ): — as mark of luxury, revelry Amos 5:23 ; 6:5 ; Amos 14:11, so 5:12 ( נ ׳כִנּוֺר חָלִיל תֹּף ), also (not in bad sense) 1Kin 10:12 ; played by wandering band of prophets 1Sam 10:5 (list as Isa 5:12 ); in worship 2Sam 6:5 ; elsewhere only Psalms, Chronicles, always in worship: Psa 57:9 ; 81:3 ; 92:4 ; 108:3 ; 150:3 ; נֶבֶל כְּלִי 71:22 ; ׳נ עָשׂוֺר a harp with ten strings 33:2 ; 144:9 ; 1Chr 13:8 ; 15:16 , 20 , 28 ; 16:5 ( נְבָלִים כְּלֵי ), 25:1 , 6 ; 2Chr 5:12 ; 9:11 ; 20:28 ; 29:25 ; Neh 12:27 . &#8212; compare further Benz Archaeology 273 ff. Now Archaeology i..273 ff. Dr Amos 234 ff. We Hpt 222 ff .","rootNote":"or נֵבֶל ; from 5034 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 13 8","keyReferences":["1Chr 13 8","1Chr 15 16","1Chr 15 20","1Chr 15 28","1Chr 16 5","1Chr 25 1","1Chr 25 6","1Kgs 10 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":38,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 13 8","book":"1Chr","chapter":13,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בִ/נְבָלִ֣ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 15 16","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נְבָלִ֥ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 15 20","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":20,"englishText":"",